(7518568, 1200873, 156466, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Dennisheckman:</b></div><hr/><i> Congrats Jake! I think you would win any "100 feet from home" challenge. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Actually, Dennis, this was closer to 7 miles from home. ;)</td>', 'Originally posted by Dennisheckman: Congrats Jake! I think you would win any "100 feet from home" challenge.   Actually, Dennis, this was closer to 7 miles from home. ;)', '2017-06-13 13:08:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(7518569, 1200873, 104230, '<td valign="top">As I commented during voting I thought this was a lovely image.  I gave it my highest vote.<br/> <br/><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=97225" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Jomari</a>''s comment<i> "It''s interesting that the leaves have the fine red border, just like the flowers" </i>  led me to share a botanical "tidbit" ... from a botanical perspective, the lovely, white, pink tinged, petal-like things that dominate the image are not flowers at all. Nor are they leaves. They are bracts. Only the small clusters in the center are flowers.<br/> <br/>I''m curious whether you knew this, as you seem pretty knowledgeable about birds and plants etc., and decided to go ahead an submit it anyway. :-) <br/> <br/>I planted some Korean dogwoods, which are much more disease resistant than the white dogwood, in the yard of my first home on the Cape. Seeing this reminds me to look into adding one in our yard here, especially since we have a fair amount of shade.<br/> <br/>Congratulations on the ribbon.</td>', 'As I commented during voting I thought this was a lovely image.  I gave it my highest vote.  Jomari''s comment "It''s interesting that the leaves have the fine red border, just like the flowers"   led me to share a botanical "tidbit" ... from a botanical perspective, the lovely, white, pink tinged, petal-like things that dominate the image are not flowers at all. Nor are they leaves. They are bracts. Only the small clusters in the center are flowers. I''m curious whether you knew this, as you seem pretty knowledgeable about birds and plants etc., and decided to go ahead an submit it anyway. :-)  I planted some Korean dogwoods, which are much more disease resistant than the white dogwood, in the yard of my first home on the Cape. Seeing this reminds me to look into adding one in our yard here, especially since we have a fair amount of shade. Congratulations on the ribbon.', '2017-06-13 13:17:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(7518571, 1200395, 175381, '<td valign="top">Beautiful color shot coach Susan. Creative composition with a nice diagonal</td>', 'Beautiful color shot coach Susan. Creative composition with a nice diagonal', '2017-06-13 13:50:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(7518582, 1200395, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge well<br/> <br/>What a lovely vibrancy you have captured here Susan. The lighting and detail is excellent, Im really intrigued how you have done it, its nicely illuminated from the front but equally appears to be backlit too? And then we have that gorgeous background which again leaves me intrigued, is it  outdoors seen through net or a soft focus patterned cloth. The shape of the flowers lends itself to your sympathetic composition nicely. All in all Susan a lovely job well done and thanks for your entry.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge well What a lovely vibrancy you have captured here Susan. The lighting and detail is excellent, Im really intrigued how you have done it, its nicely illuminated from the front but equally appears to be backlit too? And then we have that gorgeous background which again leaves me intrigued, is it  outdoors seen through net or a soft focus patterned cloth. The shape of the flowers lends itself to your sympathetic composition nicely. All in all Susan a lovely job well done and thanks for your entry.', '2017-06-13 18:34:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(7518583, 1200848, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge well<br/> <br/>A lovely portrait that is always going to appeal, very tenderly done. I have to say Im not too keen on desalt so Im pleased that you havent completely desaturated all the colour in the girl, here lovely rosy cheeks add a pleasing balance to the red of the rose. The blown highlights have hit her hair but not its a small price to pay for the important detail you have captured in her face. Its an image you will be able to treasure for a long while to come, well done Mark.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge well A lovely portrait that is always going to appeal, very tenderly done. I have to say Im not too keen on desalt so Im pleased that you havent completely desaturated all the colour in the girl, here lovely rosy cheeks add a pleasing balance to the red of the rose. The blown highlights have hit her hair but not its a small price to pay for the important detail you have captured in her face. Its an image you will be able to treasure for a long while to come, well done Mark.', '2017-06-13 18:42:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(7518584, 1200896, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge well<br/> <br/>This is all about the lighting. The lone flower nicely spotlit by the soft sunlight against the darker natural background works really well, it stands out like the attractive beacon it is. Your composition is also very complimentary to the subject and its position in the natural setting, lovely. Well taken Anton.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge well This is all about the lighting. The lone flower nicely spotlit by the soft sunlight against the darker natural background works really well, it stands out like the attractive beacon it is. Your composition is also very complimentary to the subject and its position in the natural setting, lovely. Well taken Anton.', '2017-06-13 18:46:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(7518585, 1200627, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge well<br/> <br/>What an abundance of attractive flowers. Therein lies part of the problem for me, there is just so much of it throughout the frame I am finding it a little difficult to concentrate on the main subject. I think there were two possibilities here, one to isolate the foreground and softer focus flowers against a plainer background or to isolate the front flowers alone against the distant soft focus repetitive background, for me either of these would have been more effective. However, its still a lovely entry Janine, thanks.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge well What an abundance of attractive flowers. Therein lies part of the problem for me, there is just so much of it throughout the frame I am finding it a little difficult to concentrate on the main subject. I think there were two possibilities here, one to isolate the foreground and softer focus flowers against a plainer background or to isolate the front flowers alone against the distant soft focus repetitive background, for me either of these would have been more effective. However, its still a lovely entry Janine, thanks.', '2017-06-13 18:54:00.000000', NULL, 0),
